Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: Harena Term
Upstream-Contact: Jeeyong Um <me@um.je>
Source: https://github.com/harena-hq/harena-term-font
Comment:
 This file covers what fonts-harena-term actually ships: the four compiled
 TrueType files (Files: dist/*.ttf below) and the Debian packaging itself
 (Files: debian/*). The fonts are a derivative work assembled from several
 upstream sources plus fourteen separately licensed Nerd Fonts icon sets;
 the complete provenance, per-source SHA-256 pins and a glyph-range
 breakdown of every bundled icon set are in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, which
 this package installs as documentation at
 /usr/share/doc/fonts-harena-term/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, alongside the
 full text of every non-common license referenced below under
 /usr/share/doc/fonts-harena-term/licenses/. This file does not attempt a
 copyright audit of the rest of the source repository (build scripts,
 fetched upstream sources, tooling), which is not shipped in this binary
 package.

